{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They shall not be removed from it.</b> Because of the holiness of the Ark, the Holy One, blessed be He, did not want them to handle it to remove the poles and insert them into the rings. But when they come to carry it, they hold the ends of the poles and carry it, and when they set it down they leave immediately, because of the awe of the holiness. And this is the meaning of the verse: בטבעות הארון יהיו הבדים — the poles that Moses places and fixes there, as it is written in the section ותכל, and once they are placed there — לא יסורו ממנו — they shall not be removed from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:05.267152805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}